    "text": "En caso de empate al final de un combate no concluyente, el árbitro y los cuatro jueces decidirán el combate por HANTEI.",
    "text_en": "In the event of a tied score at the end of an inconclusive bout the the Referee and the four Judges will decide the bout by HANTEI.",
    "answer": false,
    "ref": "WKF 2026.01, Art. 12.2.1, 12.2.2, 12.2.3, p. 33–34",
    "justification_en": "Official WKF Rules (WKF 2026.01, Art. 12.2.1, 12.2.2, 12.2.3, p. 33–34): Official Rule Text: \"The result of a bout is determined by... at equal score, having the first unopposed point advantage (SENSHU)... or the higher number of IPPON... higher number of WAZA ARI. Should the number of IPPON and WAZA ARI be equal, the decision will be made by HANTEI.\". Analysis: A tied score is not decided immediately by HANTEI; SENSHU, IPPON count, and WAZA-ARI count take strict precedence before HANTEI can ever be applied.",
